  "findings": [
    {
      "issue": "Idle team false Fast Moves",
      "evidence": "Moondrop inferred 1 Greninja and 3 Lucario uses; Pixel inferred 1 Lucario use. Sources are tiny HP changes and weak blue-border changes. Both devices observed the same idle team."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Camerupt wrongly assigned to player on Moondrop",
      "evidence": "Lucario faint at 123.152 s; independently read player Obstagoon at 123.330 s; Camerupt entry at 125.791 s consumed the stale player vacancy; opponent badge correctly read Camerupt at 126.839 s."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Pixel badge crops missed live resources",
      "evidence": "Resource capture availability repeatedly true but no counts entered compact archive. Saved Pixel ball crops resolve to y=165..201 in a 672x1419 retained frame while live balls sit around y=132..154. No calibration_reference directory existed. Calibration screen therefore offered bundled references in absence of user screenshots. Actual image used by user is not established. Pixel also had no overdex_screenshot_directory preferences file, so its calibration image source was the bundled references."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Pixel start and result missed",
      "evidence": "Pixel has no MatchStarted or MatchEnded. The result gate has no ball counts; only one cited countdown crop survived compact export. Moondrop recorded GO and LOSS."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Shield transitions incomplete",
      "evidence": "Moondrop recorded player shields 2 then 0, without an intermediate 1. Pixel recorded no shield counts. User confirms both shields used by Lucario."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Attacking team counts disagree",
      "evidence": "Abomasnow 39 from Moondrop opponent observations versus 29 from Pixel player observations; Camerupt 4 versus 3. Exact attack count is not established by this review."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Pixel charge announcements obscured by HUD",
      "evidence": "Pixel OCR combined Weather Ball / Energy Ball letters with HUD move lists. Only Earth Power generated a charged-energy spend; Moondrop had 4 spends, despite Pixel recording 6 charge-used episodes."
    }
  ],
